From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: prospero-win <prospero-win@invalid>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 16:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: Keep the FS base of a 64-bit thread resumed where it
 was.

The kernel restores the FS base saved in the signal frame on sigreturn,
and leave_handler replaced it with the host's whenever the frame's CS was
the 64-bit one, so that a fault from 32-bit code redirected to Wine's
64-bit exception dispatcher would not run it on the guest FS. But 64-bit
code is not always on the host FS: the native WoW64 CPU sets the guest's
with sysarch just before it switches to 32-bit code. A signal in that
window had its frame's FS base replaced, and the thread then entered its
32-bit code with the host FS; the first NtCurrentTeb() read host memory
(GTA San Andreas' DXVK workers at startup: an access violation in
RtlEnterCriticalSection reading 0xff86xxxx, the low half of the host
thread pointer).

Set the host FS base where the handler sends a context to 64-bit code it
did not interrupt: setup_raise_exception, and restore_context when the
context's CS:RIP differs from the frame's.
---
 dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c | 33 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 27 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c
index 3c17143..d5438a4 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c
@@ -974,6 +974,24 @@ static inline struct thread_data *init_handler( void *sigcontext )
 }
 
 
+#ifdef __PROSPERO__
+/* The kernel restores the FS base saved in the frame on sigreturn. A context
+ * that the handler sends to Wine's 64-bit code (the exception dispatcher, or
+ * a 64-bit context set on the thread) needs the host's. A thread resumed
+ * where it was keeps the one it had: 64-bit code is not always on the host
+ * FS, since the native WoW64 CPU sets the guest's just before it switches to
+ * 32-bit code, and forcing the host's there sent the thread into its 32-bit
+ * code with the host FS (GetCurrentThreadId reading host memory). */
+static inline void pw_set_host_fs( struct thread_data *data, ucontext_t *sigcontext )
+{
+    struct amd64_thread_data *amd64_data = amd64_thread_data( data );
+
+    if (amd64_data && amd64_data->pthread_teb && CS_sig(sigcontext) == cs64_sel)
+        FSBASE_sig(sigcontext) = (uintptr_t)amd64_data->pthread_teb;
+}
+#endif
+
+
 /***********************************************************************
  *           leave_handler
  */
@@ -982,12 +1000,6 @@ static inline void leave_handler( struct thread_data *data, ucontext_t *sigconte
     struct amd64_thread_data *amd64_data = amd64_thread_data( data );
 
     if (!amd64_data) return;
-#ifdef __PROSPERO__
-    /* The kernel restores the saved FS base on sigreturn. A fault raised
-     * from CS33 may now target Wine's CS43 exception dispatcher instead. */
-    if (CS_sig(sigcontext) == cs64_sel && amd64_data->pthread_teb)
-        FSBASE_sig(sigcontext) = (uintptr_t)amd64_data->pthread_teb;
-#endif
 #ifdef __linux__
     if (!is_inside_signal_stack( data, (void *)RSP_sig(sigcontext )) &&
         !is_inside_syscall( data, RSP_sig(sigcontext) ))
@@ -1162,6 +1174,9 @@ static void restore_context( struct thread_data *data, const struct xcontext *xc
 {
     const CONTEXT *context = &xcontext->c;
     struct amd64_thread_data *amd64_data = amd64_thread_data( data );
+#ifdef __PROSPERO__
+    BOOL resumed = RIP_sig(sigcontext) == context->Rip && CS_sig(sigcontext) == context->SegCs;
+#endif
 
     if (amd64_data)
     {
@@ -1174,6 +1189,9 @@ static void restore_context( struct thread_data *data, const struct xcontext *xc
     }
     set_sigcontext( context, sigcontext );
     if (FPU_sig(sigcontext)) memcpy( FPU_sig(sigcontext), &context->FltSave, sizeof(context->FltSave) );
+#ifdef __PROSPERO__
+    if (!resumed) pw_set_host_fs( data, sigcontext );
+#endif
     leave_handler( data, sigcontext );
 }
 
@@ -1725,6 +1743,9 @@ static void setup_raise_exception( struct thread_data *data, ucontext_t *sigcont
     }
 
     CS_sig(sigcontext)  = cs64_sel;
+#ifdef __PROSPERO__
+    pw_set_host_fs( data, sigcontext );
+#endif
     RIP_sig(sigcontext) = (ULONG_PTR)pKiUserExceptionDispatcher;
     RSP_sig(sigcontext) = (ULONG_PTR)stack;
     /* clear single-step, direction, and align check flag */
-- 
2.43.0

